        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 rounded-2xl p-8 text-gray-200">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="mb-4">
            For a plain black asphalt driveway that you want to keep black, buy a polymer-modified, sand-filled asphalt emulsion, put two coats on with a squeegee, and do it again in two or three years. It is cheap, forgiving and it looks right.
          </p>
          <p class="m-0">
            Buy acrylic when you want colour, when you are in a punishing UV climate, when fuel resistance matters, or when the driveway is a design feature worth a coating that lasts four or five years. Prepare the surface properly and apply it thin, because acrylic does not wear out gracefully, it peels.
          </p>
